## Template for `local.properties`.
##
## Copy this file to `local.properties` in the same directory and fill in your
## own values. `local.properties` is machine-specific and is git-ignored — never
## commit it.
##
##   cp local.properties.example local.properties
##
## Android Studio creates `local.properties` automatically when you open the
## project, so you usually only need to do this by hand for a command-line build.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Android SDK location
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## If this is unset, Gradle falls back to the ANDROID_HOME / ANDROID_SDK_ROOT
## environment variable, so CI runners do not need this file at all.
##
## macOS:   /Users/<you>/Library/Android/sdk
## Linux:   /home/<you>/Android/Sdk
## Windows: C:\\Users\\<you>\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\Sdk
sdk.dir=/path/to/Android/sdk

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Optional: release signing
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## When RELEASE_STORE_FILE is set, the `release` build type is signed with this
## keystore. If it is left unset, `release` builds are simply left unsigned.
##
## Keep the keystore plus these values out of version control. `*.jks`,
## `*.keystore` and `keystore/` are already git-ignored.
##
## Generate a keystore with:
##   keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore keystore/vesper-release.jks \
##     -alias vesper -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
#RELEASE_STORE_FILE=../keystore/vesper-release.jks
#RELEASE_STORE_PASSWORD=
#RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS=vesper
#RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD=
